# A raised-cosine offset: the shorter the bend, the larger the radiation loss.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title S-bend shifting a 0.5 um guide by 2 um over 20 um
window width=24 length=40
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide sbend x0=0 x1=2 width=0.5 from=10 to=30
guide straight x=2 width=0.5 from=30 to=40
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=40 x=2 width=0.5
plane end z=40
expect power out 0.999657829 2e-7
expect total end 0.999999304 2e-7
expect centroid end 2.0002782 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2843038 2e-6
expect neff 2.178196218 2e-8
